-Should he do it over?

1987
01:12:14,797 --> 01:12:16,131
It'll swell up a bit.

1988
01:12:16,432 --> 01:12:18,067
ADD THE PASTA!

1989
01:12:18,934 --> 01:12:21,537
MANTECARE ON THE MENU!

1990
01:12:21,603 --> 01:12:25,274
Mantecare<i> is an Italian word</i>
<i>that means "to mix."</i>

1991
01:12:25,341 --> 01:12:26,408
SEE THIS, JEE… HA SEOK-JIN?

1992
01:12:26,475 --> 01:12:29,044
COOK LIKE A CHEF
LESSON 6: MANTECARE IS A MUST FOR PASTA!

1993
01:12:29,111 --> 01:12:30,112
Five minutes!

1994
01:12:30,179 --> 01:12:32,681
Jung-hwan, please report from the kitchen.

1995
01:12:32,748 --> 01:12:34,516
It's the first Italian derby in a while.

1996
01:12:35,317 --> 01:12:36,151
Sesame oil?

1997
01:12:36,218 --> 01:12:37,052
Nice.

1998
01:12:37,853 --> 01:12:41,023
Will Sam destroy Sung-jun's spirit?

1999
01:12:41,090 --> 01:12:42,691
-Breadcrumbs?
-Breadcrumbs.

2000
01:12:42,758 --> 01:12:45,094
-Breadcrumbs.
-Sung-jun's breadcrumbs are ready.

2001
01:12:45,160 --> 01:12:46,929
German breadcrumbs.

2002
01:12:46,995 --> 01:12:48,364
-The meat mix.
-German breadcrumbs.

2003
01:12:48,430 --> 01:12:49,565
The meat mixture.

2004
01:12:49,631 --> 01:12:51,734
You have to deep-fry these, right?

2005
01:12:51,800 --> 01:12:53,068
Sung-jun looks focused.

2006
01:12:53,135 --> 01:12:54,937
-Are you leaving the pasta like this?
-Yes.

2007
01:12:56,705 --> 01:12:57,539
That's so cool.

2008
01:12:57,606 --> 01:12:59,475
-No flour, though?
-He's looking cool.

2009
01:12:59,541 --> 01:13:01,610
WATCH CLOSELY!

2010
01:13:01,677 --> 01:13:03,178
Give him a look.

2011
01:13:03,245 --> 01:13:04,413
LIKE THIS

2012
01:13:04,480 --> 01:13:05,848
Are you watching him, Jee Seok-jin?

2013
01:13:05,914 --> 01:13:07,583
COMEDY IS ALL ABOUT REPETITION!

2014
01:13:07,850 --> 01:13:10,652
AGAIN, WE APOLOGIZE,
BOTH HA SEOK-JIN AND JEE SEOK-JIN

2015
01:13:10,719 --> 01:13:11,620
I'm sorry!

2016
01:13:12,121 --> 01:13:15,391
It's time to coat them
with breadcrumbs and deep-fry.

2017
01:13:15,457 --> 01:13:17,059
He's coating it with breadcrumbs.

2018
01:13:18,093 --> 01:13:20,462
-The oil doesn't look hot enough.
-It doesn't?

2019
01:13:21,663 --> 01:13:22,564
It's working.

2020
01:13:22,631 --> 01:13:24,032
-It's high enough.
-Is it?

2021
01:13:24,099 --> 01:13:26,535
-Actually, it's a bit too high.
-It's too high.

2022
01:13:26,602 --> 01:13:28,570
DROPPING THE TEMPERATURE

2023
01:13:28,637 --> 01:13:30,172
Take them out and try again.

2024
01:13:30,806 --> 01:13:32,074
It looks fine now.

2025
01:13:32,574 --> 01:13:35,110
Jung-hwan, why don't you try the pasta?

2026
01:13:35,177 --> 01:13:37,479
Sung-jun's pasta.

2027
01:13:37,546 --> 01:13:38,814
-Parmesan.
-The sauce.

2028
01:13:39,381 --> 01:13:42,551
Does it taste like
he doesn't know how to lose?

2029
01:13:43,118 --> 01:13:44,253
GULP

2030
01:13:44,319 --> 01:13:46,054
It seems so, but…

2031
01:13:46,255 --> 01:13:47,556
BUT?

2032
01:13:47,623 --> 01:13:49,625
…why does it taste like bulgogi?

2033
01:13:49,691 --> 01:13:51,560
He added sesame oil.

2034
01:13:52,161 --> 01:13:53,896
No, it's <i>mazesoba.</i>

2035
01:13:53,962 --> 01:13:56,165
<i>-Mazesoba?</i>
-It's mixed pasta.

2036
01:13:56,231 --> 01:13:57,466
Is it supposed to be like bulgogi?

2037
01:13:57,533 --> 01:13:59,568
-He added sesame oil.
-He added sesame oil.

2038
01:13:59,635 --> 01:14:01,570
-It tastes like bulgogi to me.
-It's the sesame oil.

2039
01:14:01,637 --> 01:14:02,671
But it's good.

2040
01:14:02,738 --> 01:14:04,773
-He's making it in a different way.
-Okay!

2041
01:14:04,973 --> 01:14:06,275
AS REQUESTED, WHITE BALSAMIC VINEGAR

2042
01:14:06,341 --> 01:14:09,178
-I have a bad feeling about it.
-He requested that they use it.

2043
01:14:09,244 --> 01:14:11,713
You add rice vinegar to <i>mazesoba,</i> right?

2044
01:14:11,780 --> 01:14:12,781
-Yes.
-He's doing that.

2045
01:14:12,848 --> 01:14:14,383
It'll taste pretty good

2046
01:14:14,450 --> 01:14:15,951
with a raw egg yolk on top.

2047
01:14:16,018 --> 01:14:17,453
I think Sung-jun's pasta is ready.

2048
01:14:17,519 --> 01:14:19,154
He's plating the pasta.

2049
01:14:19,221 --> 01:14:21,990
-That's his pasta.
-You have 1 minute and 40 seconds.

2050
01:14:22,057 --> 01:14:23,459
Sung-jun's pasta is ready.

2051
01:14:24,026 --> 01:14:25,060
BARELY ENOUGH TIME

2052
01:14:25,127 --> 01:14:27,596
He's now waiting for the oven.
What's that?

2053
01:14:27,663 --> 01:14:29,064
It's butter.

2054
01:14:29,131 --> 01:14:29,965
Butter.

2055
01:14:30,032 --> 01:14:33,435
-What are you cooking right now?
-The sauce.

2056
01:14:33,502 --> 01:14:36,038
-Can you try that sauce?
-This sauce.

2057
01:14:36,104 --> 01:14:38,640
-The sauce.
-The canine sauce!

2058
01:14:38,707 --> 01:14:40,676
-The problematic sauce!
-The problematic sauce!

2059
01:14:41,710 --> 01:14:46,048
Does it taste like
he'll teach Sung-jun how to lose?

2060
01:14:46,114 --> 01:14:48,283
He'll definitely teach him how.

2061
01:14:48,350 --> 01:14:50,185
SAM KIM THE STAR INSTRUCTOR!

2062
01:14:50,652 --> 01:14:51,920
It's very smooth.

2063
01:14:51,987 --> 01:14:53,255
What did you add? Mushrooms?

2064
01:14:53,322 --> 01:14:55,858
I used the mushroom pasta sauce.

2065
01:14:55,924 --> 01:14:57,759
-It tastes so good.
-Sam uses the sauce.

2066
01:14:57,826 --> 01:14:59,561
-He used that?
-The Italian round.

2067
01:14:59,628 --> 01:15:01,330
One minute left.

2068
01:15:01,396 --> 01:15:03,398
It'll be tough for him to choose.

2069
01:15:03,665 --> 01:15:05,534
WHAT WILL COME OUT
FROM THE PROBLEMATIC OVEN?

2070
01:15:05,601 --> 01:15:07,302
-What's that?
-One minute left.

2071
01:15:08,136 --> 01:15:10,305
The seasoned pork he made.

2072
01:15:10,372 --> 01:15:12,441
He put that in the oven?

2073
01:15:12,508 --> 01:15:14,476
Is that <i>chashu?</i>

2074
01:15:14,543 --> 01:15:15,811
Is this the topping?

2075
01:15:15,878 --> 01:15:17,579
-Yes, it's like <i>chashu.</i>
<i>-Chashu.</i>

2076
01:15:20,082 --> 01:15:21,650
WHAT'S IN SAM'S OVEN?

2077
01:15:21,717 --> 01:15:23,585
The Wellington is ready.

2078
01:15:23,652 --> 01:15:26,388
Wait, you have no time. Forty seconds.

2079
01:15:27,623 --> 01:15:30,893
8. PULL THE WELLINGNULL OUT OF THE OVEN
AND SEAR IT WITH A TORCH

2080
01:15:30,959 --> 01:15:32,261
The gas won't work.

2081
01:15:33,328 --> 01:15:34,630
It got on the paper!

2082
01:15:36,765 --> 01:15:38,200
The paper makes it smoky?

2083
01:15:40,068 --> 01:15:41,570
EGG

2084
01:15:41,637 --> 01:15:43,539
Twenty seconds.

2085
01:15:43,605 --> 01:15:44,873
Twenty seconds.

2086
01:15:44,940 --> 01:15:46,475
The sauce is boiling.

2087
01:15:46,542 --> 01:15:49,578
10. TOP PASTA WITH EGG YOLK,
SEASONED ROASTED SEAWEED, AND CILANTRO

2088
01:15:49,645 --> 01:15:50,712
Sesame seeds.

2089
01:15:50,779 --> 01:15:52,414
-Sesame seeds.
-Sprinkle it on top.

2090
01:15:52,581 --> 01:15:53,415
GROUND SESAME SEED

2091
01:15:54,616 --> 01:15:56,351
What about this?

2092
01:15:56,418 --> 01:15:57,953
I have to get it out.

2093
01:15:58,020 --> 01:15:59,788
-Nine. Eight.
-Nine. Eight.

2094
01:15:59,855 --> 01:16:01,790
-Seven. Six.
-Seven. Six.

2095
01:16:01,857 --> 01:16:03,225
Ten seconds!

2096
01:16:03,926 --> 01:16:06,295
PLATING THE DISH
WITH ONLY 10 SECONDS LEFT!

2097
01:16:06,628 --> 01:16:09,932
SMOOTH CREAM SAUCE!

2098
01:16:11,600 --> 01:16:13,435
SEA URCHIN ROE

2099
01:16:13,635 --> 01:16:15,170
WOBBLY

2100
01:16:15,237 --> 01:16:17,172
-Ring it first.
-The bell!

2101
01:16:17,239 --> 01:16:18,473
Ring the bell first!

2102
01:16:18,540 --> 01:16:20,509
-Ring it first.
-The bell!

2103
01:16:20,576 --> 01:16:21,777
TIME'S UP!

2104
01:16:21,843 --> 01:16:24,313
-Sam finishes first.
-Sam finishes.

2105
01:16:24,379 --> 01:16:26,748
-Sam's done.
-He topped it with sea urchin roe?

2106
01:16:26,815 --> 01:16:28,684
-He topped it with sea urchin roe.
-He did.

2107
01:16:28,750 --> 01:16:31,320
-Sung-jun is done too.
-He's done.

2108
01:16:31,386 --> 01:16:32,788
SUNG-JUN FINISHES MANTECARE ON THE MENU

2109
01:16:32,854 --> 01:16:34,323
Wow.

2110
01:16:34,957 --> 01:16:37,993
DISHES WITH A GREEN TOUCH

2111
01:16:38,060 --> 01:16:41,029
They both worked on
timely dishes this time.

2112
01:16:41,096 --> 01:16:42,531
It's impossible in 15 minutes.

2113
01:16:42,598 --> 01:16:43,432
These meat dishes.

2114
01:16:43,498 --> 01:16:45,634
It's crazy.

2115
01:16:45,701 --> 01:16:49,471
And now, both dishes were made
to fill Seok-jin's order.

2116
01:16:49,538 --> 01:16:52,407
The 15 minutes went by so quickly.

2117
01:16:52,474 --> 01:16:54,843
You're playing an Italian chef,

2118
01:16:54,910 --> 01:16:57,346
so we thought you'd have
a lot of to learn in this round.

2119
01:16:57,412 --> 01:16:59,314
At first, they offered to teach you,

2120
01:16:59,381 --> 01:17:02,117
but one of them
even called you Jee Seok-jin.

2121
01:17:02,184 --> 01:17:05,087
He didn't even show you how to <i>mantecare.</i>

2122
01:17:05,153 --> 01:17:08,957
Also, there is a bit of a problem

2123
01:17:09,024 --> 01:17:11,393
-that I wish to pose.
-What is it?

2124
01:17:11,460 --> 01:17:13,595
Before the round started,

2125
01:17:13,662 --> 01:17:16,798
<i>Sung-jun went to the oven and said,</i>
<i>"Who turned off the oven?"</i>

2126
01:17:16,865 --> 01:17:18,433
THE OVEN WAS TURNED OFF

2127
01:17:18,500 --> 01:17:19,901
-Yes.
-Did you see that?

2128
01:17:19,968 --> 01:17:21,970
It reminded me of something else.

2129
01:17:22,037 --> 01:17:23,138
-What is it?
-What?

2130
01:17:23,205 --> 01:17:24,906
Once before, Chef Ho-young

2131
01:17:24,973 --> 01:17:28,543
also suffered because
someone had turned off the fridge.

2132
01:17:28,610 --> 01:17:30,112
I think the freezer's broken.

2133
01:17:30,846 --> 01:17:32,714
THE DAY WHEN HE MADE BINGO MANGSU

2134
01:17:32,781 --> 01:17:34,316
Yes, right.

2135
01:17:34,383 --> 01:17:36,351
-The day he made bingo mangsu.
-Wait, no.

2136
01:17:36,418 --> 01:17:38,654
And oddly, his opponent that day

2137
01:17:38,720 --> 01:17:39,921
was also Sam Kim.

2138
01:17:40,656 --> 01:17:42,391
-Sam Kim.
-What?

2139
01:17:43,058 --> 01:17:44,326
Oh, my gosh!

2140
01:17:44,693 --> 01:17:45,794
IS THIS A COINCIDENCE?

2141
01:17:45,861 --> 01:17:46,995
Is it just me?

2142
01:17:47,062 --> 01:17:48,563
-My gosh.
-Gosh.

2143
01:17:48,630 --> 01:17:50,399
-When the freezer went out,
-Really?

2144
01:17:50,465 --> 01:17:52,501
<i>…he was playing against Sam.</i>

2145
01:17:52,567 --> 01:17:53,735
Was that his strategy?

2146
01:17:53,802 --> 01:17:54,903
I hoped it wouldn't be.

2147
01:17:54,970 --> 01:17:56,738
As soon as I got here today,

2148
01:17:56,805 --> 01:17:59,241
he asked me for the circuit box.

2149
01:17:59,307 --> 01:18:00,542
Did he really?

2150
01:18:00,609 --> 01:18:03,845
Yes, I wondered why he wanted to know.

2151
01:18:03,912 --> 01:18:05,514
I'm getting chills.

2152
01:18:05,580 --> 01:18:06,581
He asked me too.

2153
01:18:06,648 --> 01:18:08,917
"Do you think I can
cut the wire with my canine?"

2154
01:18:10,519 --> 01:18:11,386
TOO MUCH…

2155
01:18:11,453 --> 01:18:12,654
I'm dead serious.

2156
01:18:12,721 --> 01:18:13,755
Wow.

2157
01:18:13,822 --> 01:18:15,691
Was that how you were using your canine?

2158
01:18:15,757 --> 01:18:18,060
-I see.
-Who turned it off?

2159
01:18:18,126 --> 01:18:21,163
Was this Sam's grand plan? Nobody knows.

2160
01:18:21,229 --> 01:18:22,898
If he wins again today,

2161
01:18:22,964 --> 01:18:24,433
this is bound to happen often.

2162
01:18:25,300 --> 01:18:27,669
Careful, everyone. Watch out.

2163
01:18:27,736 --> 01:18:30,272
Now, Sam finished first.

2164
01:18:30,338 --> 01:18:31,473
<i>Beef WellingNull.</i>

2165
01:18:31,540 --> 01:18:37,746
BEEF WELLINGNULL
TO MAKE THE MEAT IN THE FRIDGE NULL

2166
01:18:38,447 --> 01:18:42,617
CHEF SAM KIM'S BEEF WELLINGNULL

2167
01:18:43,051 --> 01:18:44,586
SMELLS IT FIRST

2168
01:18:45,387 --> 01:18:46,688
It smells so good.

2169
01:18:46,755 --> 01:18:48,490
-Does it?
-First of all,

2170
01:18:48,557 --> 01:18:52,027
-see how well the meat is cooked.
-I'll cut it.

2171
01:18:52,094 --> 01:18:53,962
-Wow.
-It must be nicely cooked.

2172
01:18:54,396 --> 01:18:55,797
CUTTING

2173
01:18:56,164 --> 01:18:57,733
ALL EYES ON THE DISH

2174
01:18:57,799 --> 01:18:59,768
He'll see meat inside.

2175
01:19:02,137 --> 01:19:03,338
IS THIS COOKED?

2176
01:19:03,405 --> 01:19:04,840
-It's cooked.
-Is it cooked nicely?

2177
01:19:04,906 --> 01:19:06,808
When you make Wellington,

2178
01:19:06,875 --> 01:19:08,910
you can't have the meat well done.

2179
01:19:08,977 --> 01:19:10,612
It has to be a little rare.

2180
01:19:10,679 --> 01:19:11,646
I see.

2181
01:19:11,713 --> 01:19:15,684
He hasn't been cooking meat at home
after the holiday trauma.

2182
01:19:17,018 --> 01:19:18,620
TAKING A BIG BITE

2183
01:19:18,687 --> 01:19:19,788
He takes a big bite.

2184
01:19:20,789 --> 01:19:21,957
SOFT GAZE

2185
01:19:22,190 --> 01:19:23,492
WHOA

2186
01:19:23,558 --> 01:19:25,694
He glances at Sam for a brief moment.

2187
01:19:25,761 --> 01:19:27,028
Emergency.

2188
01:19:29,865 --> 01:19:31,700
OH, LOOK AT THIS THING

2189
01:19:33,602 --> 01:19:35,070
He truly is an old dude.

2190
01:19:35,137 --> 01:19:37,139
He stares at the food when it's delicious.

2191
01:19:37,205 --> 01:19:38,373
OLD DUDE STARTER PACK: STARES AT GOOD FOOD

2192
01:19:40,108 --> 01:19:41,276
Man.

2193
01:19:41,343 --> 01:19:44,012
ANOTHER BITE WHILE STARING

2194
01:19:44,780 --> 01:19:47,048
He savors the dish quietly.

2195
01:19:47,115 --> 01:19:48,416
What is it?

2196
01:19:48,483 --> 01:19:51,253
-What's this bouncy texture?
-The bouncy texture?

2197
01:19:51,319 --> 01:19:53,488
Wellington is made

2198
01:19:53,555 --> 01:19:57,259
<i>with beef tenderloin wrapped with ham.</i>

2199
01:19:57,325 --> 01:20:00,095
You had beef brisket,
so I used it to create a similar texture.

2200
01:20:00,162 --> 01:20:03,131
<i>That's probably the bouncy texture.</i>

2201
01:20:03,198 --> 01:20:06,701
Beef brisket… It must be the one here.

2202
01:20:07,068 --> 01:20:08,136
THIS TIME, JUST THE MEAT

2203
01:20:08,203 --> 01:20:09,738
Does it go well with the meat?

2204
01:20:09,805 --> 01:20:11,072
Yes, it does.

2205
01:20:11,139 --> 01:20:13,341
<i>And the sauce has a dash of sourness,</i>

2206
01:20:14,409 --> 01:20:17,245
which balances out the greasiness.

2207
01:20:17,312 --> 01:20:19,214
I made it with mustard,

2208
01:20:19,281 --> 01:20:21,516
<i>-so it must be that.</i>
<i>-I guess so.</i>

2209
01:20:21,583 --> 01:20:24,252
<i>And I saw him spread it</i>
<i>on the pie dough too.</i>

2210
01:20:25,687 --> 01:20:26,521
SLURP

2211
01:20:28,490 --> 01:20:29,791
-Gosh.
-Another bite.

2212
01:20:29,858 --> 01:20:33,695
-He wolfs it down.
-He must've wanted to eat meat badly.

2213
01:20:34,830 --> 01:20:36,498
Gosh. This is good.

2214
01:20:36,565 --> 01:20:38,667
I see. Look how happy he is.

2215
01:20:38,733 --> 01:20:41,136
Old dudes always look up.

2216
01:20:41,203 --> 01:20:42,470
OLD DUDE STARTER PACK:
LOOKS UP WHEN IMPRESSED

2217
01:20:42,537 --> 01:20:43,672
Either the ground or the sky.

2218
01:20:43,738 --> 01:20:45,640
-That was delicious.
-All right.

2219
01:20:45,707 --> 01:20:48,009
-So this is what it's like.
-He looks pleased.

2220
01:20:48,076 --> 01:20:50,412
Next, Chef Sung-jun's dish,

2221
01:20:50,478 --> 01:20:52,480
Mantecare<i> on the Menu.</i>

2222
01:20:52,547 --> 01:20:57,786
MIXED PASTA MADE
WITH A VARIETY OF GROUND MEAT

2223
01:20:58,687 --> 01:21:04,226
GROUND MEAT CUTLET WITH SEA URCHIN ROE

2224
01:21:05,594 --> 01:21:09,264
CHEF KWON SUNG-JUN'S MANTECARE ON THE MENU

2225
01:21:09,331 --> 01:21:11,833
This is Japanese-style mixed pasta.

2226
01:21:11,900 --> 01:21:16,104
He basically likes
everything that's ramen.

2227
01:21:16,171 --> 01:21:17,939
The noodles look so good.

2228
01:21:18,006 --> 01:21:20,141
-But it's pasta.
-It'll taste nice with that sour note.

2229
01:21:20,208 --> 01:21:21,810
Japanese-style mixed pasta.

2230
01:21:23,411 --> 01:21:24,246
Hmm?

2231
01:21:24,312 --> 01:21:26,615
Jung-hwan said
it tasted like bulgogi sauce.

2232
01:21:27,215 --> 01:21:28,416
YUM

2233
01:21:28,483 --> 01:21:30,051
-Cilantro?
-Cilantro.

2234
01:21:30,118 --> 01:21:31,887
Yes, I like that cilantro smell.

2235
01:21:31,953 --> 01:21:35,590
Cilantro changed the flavor
that could've been too cliché.

2236
01:21:35,657 --> 01:21:37,325
What do you mean by cliché?

2237
01:21:37,392 --> 01:21:38,827
As you said, bulgogi.

2238
01:21:38,894 --> 01:21:40,595
Right? It tastes like bulgogi.

2239
01:21:40,662 --> 01:21:41,796
It feels more like

2240
01:21:41,863 --> 01:21:44,032
Korean cuisine, actually.

2241
01:21:44,099 --> 01:21:45,767
He poured in sesame oil.

2242
01:21:45,834 --> 01:21:47,669
He's facing a danger.

2243
01:21:47,736 --> 01:21:49,170
-Emergency.
-Yes.

2244
01:21:49,237 --> 01:21:51,139
-Where's the light?
-It's an emergency.

2245
01:21:51,206 --> 01:21:52,307
Where's the light?

2246
01:21:52,374 --> 01:21:53,942
He gets rid of it when he cooks.

2247
01:21:54,009 --> 01:21:55,577
He carries it on him?

2248
01:21:55,644 --> 01:21:56,978
The emergency light is mine.

2249
01:21:57,045 --> 01:21:58,813
We should've turned it on now.

2250
01:21:58,880 --> 01:22:00,548
-To not let anyone else use it?
-He took it?

2251
01:22:00,615 --> 01:22:02,851
You were trying to make
bulgogi pasta, right?

2252
01:22:02,918 --> 01:22:05,420
I'm a guy who's Korean to his core, so…

2253
01:22:05,720 --> 01:22:06,988
ANALYZING…

2254
01:22:07,055 --> 01:22:08,623
He's nervous right now.

2255
01:22:09,858 --> 01:22:11,693
-You're so nervous.
-He's in a crisis.

2256
01:22:11,760 --> 01:22:13,061
Try the ground beef cutlets.

2257
01:22:13,128 --> 01:22:14,863
He tries to get him
to try the beef cutlets.

2258
01:22:15,597 --> 01:22:17,966
-I wonder if it's fully cooked.
-I don't think so.

2259
01:22:18,033 --> 01:22:19,334
-I doubt it.
-It's cooked.

2260
01:22:19,401 --> 01:22:20,402
It can't be reddish.

2261
01:22:20,936 --> 01:22:21,903
Is it cooked?

2262
01:22:21,970 --> 01:22:23,905
-It's fully cooked.
-It is?

2263
01:22:23,972 --> 01:22:24,806
It's fully cooked.

2264
01:22:26,141 --> 01:22:27,309
It continued to cook.

2265
01:22:28,476 --> 01:22:30,211
-I wasn't so sure before.
-Right?

2266
01:22:30,278 --> 01:22:32,614
-Thank goodness you rang the bell later.
-Yes, it's thanks to that.

2267
01:22:33,882 --> 01:22:37,085
Between the two dishes,
which one would you put

2268
01:22:37,152 --> 01:22:38,320
a bigger emphasis on?

2269
01:22:38,386 --> 01:22:40,188
It's obvious, because the topic

2270
01:22:40,255 --> 01:22:41,957
was Problematic Meat.

2271
01:22:42,023 --> 01:22:45,160
The dish that was made
to use up these problematic meats

2272
01:22:45,226 --> 01:22:46,428
was the beef cutlet.

2273
01:22:46,494 --> 01:22:47,929
That's the main dish.

2274
01:22:47,996 --> 01:22:49,464
I see. So the pasta goes?

2275
01:22:49,531 --> 01:22:52,534
I only made the pasta to show Seok-jin

2276
01:22:52,600 --> 01:22:54,135
my techniques.

2277
01:22:54,202 --> 01:22:56,271
-To teach him how to <i>mantecare</i>.
-As an example?

2278
01:22:56,338 --> 01:22:58,206
He's lying right now.

2279
01:22:58,707 --> 01:23:01,977
-Is that his lying face?
-That's not the case.

2280
01:23:02,777 --> 01:23:04,879
He claims
the beef cutlet is the main dish.

2281
01:23:06,348 --> 01:23:07,716
They're topped with sea urchin roe.

2282
01:23:08,216 --> 01:23:10,652
Will the fish roe
go well with the beef cutlets?

2283
01:23:10,719 --> 01:23:12,754
-Let me try another bite.
-One more bite.

2284
01:23:12,821 --> 01:23:15,390
-This isn't…
-I guess he's not sure yet.

2285
01:23:15,457 --> 01:23:16,925
He has another bite.

2286
01:23:16,992 --> 01:23:18,493
I guess it's somewhat…

2287
01:23:19,728 --> 01:23:20,962
CAREFUL…

2288
01:23:21,029 --> 01:23:23,198
Is it good or…

2289
01:23:23,264 --> 01:23:25,834
We aren't sure if that is
a positive or a negative response.

2290
01:23:25,900 --> 01:23:27,002
Is it the seasoning?

2291
01:23:27,068 --> 01:23:29,070
Did you not make it with sauce…

2292
01:23:29,137 --> 01:23:30,171
You're eating it yourself.

2293
01:23:30,972 --> 01:23:31,906
What are you doing?

2294
01:23:31,973 --> 01:23:33,475
He's suddenly eating it himself.

2295
01:23:33,541 --> 01:23:35,343
That's mine. Stop eating.

2296
01:23:35,410 --> 01:23:37,912
What were you checking for, Sung-jun?

2297
01:23:37,979 --> 01:23:39,247
Well,

2298
01:23:39,314 --> 01:23:40,949
he didn't say much, so I tried it.

2299
01:23:42,384 --> 01:23:43,785
-He's anxious.
-"Why is he so quiet?"

2300
01:23:43,852 --> 01:23:45,920
-It tastes good.
-"I think it's good."

2301
01:23:45,987 --> 01:23:49,357
Because it's not easy to make
such a tender ground beef cutlet.

2302
01:23:49,424 --> 01:23:50,825
-Really?
-It's nice and juicy.

2303
01:23:50,892 --> 01:23:52,260
It is good.

2304
01:23:52,327 --> 01:23:54,963
Let me ask you once more.
What's the main dish? Pasta or cutlets?

2305
01:23:55,030 --> 01:23:57,465
-Give him your answer.
-Choose wisely.

2306
01:23:57,532 --> 01:23:58,933
THINKING…

2307
01:23:59,000 --> 01:24:01,369
After all, I'm an Italian chef…

2308
01:24:01,736 --> 01:24:03,905
OF COURSE, IT'S THE PASTA

2309
01:24:03,972 --> 01:24:06,207
While he thinks about it,

2310
01:24:06,274 --> 01:24:08,109
we should let Yeo-jeong try some too.

2311
01:24:08,176 --> 01:24:10,011
Yeo-jeong will try the dish.

2312
01:24:10,078 --> 01:24:12,147
Will she also like these dishes?

2313
01:24:12,213 --> 01:24:14,549
He put a lot of work into the sauce.

2314
01:24:14,616 --> 01:24:15,884
A BIG BITE

2315
01:24:17,886 --> 01:24:19,888
TWO THUMBS UP

2316
01:24:20,455 --> 01:24:21,356
This is so good.

2317
01:24:21,423 --> 01:24:22,857
She says, "This is so good."

2318
01:24:22,924 --> 01:24:24,526
How did the pie sheet turn out so tender?

2319
01:24:24,592 --> 01:24:27,829
<i>I made it as thin as possible.</i>

2320
01:24:27,896 --> 01:24:29,631
<i>-That's why it's tender.</i>
<i>-I see.</i>

2321
01:24:29,697 --> 01:24:32,801
And the mustard he spread inside
was a really good kick.

2322
01:24:32,867 --> 01:24:34,569
He used truffle-flavored mustard,

2323
01:24:34,636 --> 01:24:38,506
so it can intensify the meat flavor.

2324
01:24:38,573 --> 01:24:39,474
He brought it up.

2325
01:24:39,541 --> 01:24:41,543
Next, Chef Sung-jun's dish.

2326
01:24:41,609 --> 01:24:43,111
I was curious about these noodles.

2327
01:24:43,411 --> 01:24:44,712
SLURP

2328
01:24:44,779 --> 01:24:46,281
LOL

2329
01:24:47,148 --> 01:24:48,283
Is it bulgogi noodles?

2330
01:24:48,349 --> 01:24:49,451
What do you think?

2331
01:24:50,418 --> 01:24:51,686
This bulgogi is delicious.

2332
01:24:52,620 --> 01:24:54,556
-Bulgogi is the best.
-"This bulgogi is delicious."

2333
01:24:54,622 --> 01:24:55,857
Eonyang bulgogi pasta.

2334
01:24:55,924 --> 01:24:57,325
Open up a Korean restaurant.

2335
01:24:57,392 --> 01:24:59,094
-I knew it.
-It's so good.

2336
01:24:59,160 --> 01:25:01,062
Next, ground beef cutlets
with sea urchin roe.

2337
01:25:02,163 --> 01:25:03,131
YUM

2338
01:25:04,866 --> 01:25:06,835
A CLOSER LOOK…

2339
01:25:09,671 --> 01:25:10,672
NERVOUS

2340
01:25:10,738 --> 01:25:12,507
Do you feel thirsty? Is it too dry?

2341
01:25:12,574 --> 01:25:13,942
It's quite tender.

2342
01:25:14,008 --> 01:25:15,643
It's not dry at all, but…

2343
01:25:15,710 --> 01:25:17,345
-What is it?
-But?

2344
01:25:17,412 --> 01:25:20,482
But I keep wondering
if he served it with anything else.

2345
01:25:20,548 --> 01:25:23,785
If I may tell you this frankly,

2346
01:25:23,852 --> 01:25:24,719
it's not salty enough.

2347
01:25:24,786 --> 01:25:27,455
Because this dish had a strong flavor,

2348
01:25:27,522 --> 01:25:29,824
-this tastes more bland in comparison.
-You're right.

2349
01:25:29,891 --> 01:25:32,327
He should've seasoned it more.

2350
01:25:32,393 --> 01:25:35,296
Sam, what kind of state
is Sung-jun in right now?

2351
01:25:36,164 --> 01:25:37,565
He has checked out.

2352
01:25:39,501 --> 01:25:42,403
PRETTY MUCH A MIND READER

2353
01:25:43,171 --> 01:25:45,974
You know Sung-jun too well.

2354
01:25:46,040 --> 01:25:48,243
It was about time he checked out.

2355
01:25:48,610 --> 01:25:50,111
NODDING…

2356
01:25:50,178 --> 01:25:51,546
He looks like he has given up.

2357
01:25:51,613 --> 01:25:54,449
All right, now. Problematic Meat.

2358
01:25:54,516 --> 01:25:56,718
<i>Press one for Sung-jun</i>

2359
01:25:56,784 --> 01:25:59,487
<i>and two for Sam. Goodness.</i>

2360
01:25:59,554 --> 01:26:01,656
Sung-jun's win rate had been great so far.

2361
01:26:01,723 --> 01:26:04,559
But he has his eyes closed right now.

2362
01:26:04,626 --> 01:26:07,462
It looks like he has let many things go.

2363
01:26:07,529 --> 01:26:08,997
You never know.

2364
01:26:09,063 --> 01:26:09,964
Did you choose one?

2365
01:26:10,999 --> 01:26:12,467
-I did.
-He did.

2366
01:26:12,534 --> 01:26:16,738
He even turned off
the power for Sung-jun's oven.

2367
01:26:17,705 --> 01:26:19,974
We might see him
on a true crime channel soon.

2368
01:26:20,275 --> 01:26:21,776
1. A FAMOUS CHEF
HABITUALLY TURNS OFF POWER

2369
01:26:21,843 --> 01:26:23,378
<i>We'll see him in one of the episodes.</i>

2370
01:26:23,444 --> 01:26:26,381
We'll investigate
what happened today after the shoot.

2371
01:26:26,447 --> 01:26:28,082
I need the video replay.

2372
01:26:28,149 --> 01:26:29,551
Problematic Meat.

2373
01:26:29,617 --> 01:26:32,220
Which dish did Seok-jin choose? Show us!

2374
01:26:33,555 --> 01:26:38,459
Sung-jun has been on a roll lately,
not knowing what the word "losing" means.

2375
01:26:38,526 --> 01:26:41,162
But Sam is here to tell him how to lose.

2376
01:26:41,229 --> 01:26:44,399
Which dish did Seok-jin choose?

2377
01:26:44,465 --> 01:26:46,935
What's the result for Problematic Meat?

2378
01:26:47,969 --> 01:26:49,971
SAM KIM WINS

2379
01:26:50,305 --> 01:26:51,806
CHEF SAM KIM'S BEEF WELLINGNULL WINS

2380
01:26:51,873 --> 01:26:52,707
It was Sam.

2381
01:26:53,141 --> 01:26:56,010
SAM WINS WITHOUT A TWIST!

2382
01:26:57,011 --> 01:26:58,947
There will be a controversy.

2383
01:27:01,649 --> 01:27:03,051
The thing is,

2384
01:27:03,985 --> 01:27:07,455
if Chef Sung-jun had finished first

2385
01:27:07,522 --> 01:27:11,226
and I got to try the cutlets, noodles,
and then the Wellington,

2386
01:27:11,292 --> 01:27:14,229
-the result would've changed drastically.
-I see.

2387
01:27:14,295 --> 01:27:18,433
Chef Sam's dish
left such a strong impression.

2388
01:27:18,499 --> 01:27:20,001
Let me ask you one last time.

2389
01:27:20,868 --> 01:27:22,403
Did you tamper with the oven?

2390
01:27:24,572 --> 01:27:26,241
I'll let you know in the next episode.

2391
01:27:26,908 --> 01:27:28,810
He's good.

2392
01:27:29,244 --> 01:27:30,945
APPROVED

2393
01:27:31,012 --> 01:27:32,647
We can do a back-and-forth now.

2394
01:27:32,714 --> 01:27:34,849
I believe we must get down
to the root of the problem.

2395
01:27:34,916 --> 01:27:36,584
Yes, it's frightening.

2396
01:27:36,651 --> 01:27:38,086
Please leave the kitchen as is.

2397
01:27:38,152 --> 01:27:40,788
We'll have a forensics team come by,

2398
01:27:40,855 --> 01:27:42,056
so don't touch anything.

2399
01:27:42,123 --> 01:27:44,058
Leave everything as is before you go.

2400
01:27:44,125 --> 01:27:46,728
Can you reinvestigate my cook-off too?

2401
01:27:46,794 --> 01:27:48,796
-Even Ho-young's round?
-Reinvestigate?

2402
01:27:48,863 --> 01:27:50,932
We will take that into consideration.

2403
01:27:50,999 --> 01:27:52,600
HEHE

2404
01:27:52,667 --> 01:27:54,302
Please put a star on Sam.

2405
01:27:55,570 --> 01:27:57,939
-Great job.
-Seok-jin chose Chef Sam.

2406
01:27:58,006 --> 01:28:02,110
That's Sam's eighth star!

2407
01:28:02,677 --> 01:28:04,646
Congratulations, Sam.

2408
01:28:04,712 --> 01:28:07,982
COMING UP: JONATHAN & PATRICIA,
BIBI & NAKYOUNG'S PREVIEW

2409
01:28:08,383 --> 01:28:10,952
Please welcome today's fridge owners!

2410
01:28:11,019 --> 01:28:12,353
The sisters, BIBI and NaKyoung,

2411
01:28:12,420 --> 01:28:14,155
and the siblings, Jonathan and Patricia.

2412
01:28:14,222 --> 01:28:16,391
-We kiss each other on the cheek.
-I can do it now.

2413
01:28:16,591 --> 01:28:17,692
THE TWO LOVING SISTERS

2414
01:28:18,059 --> 01:28:19,060
LEAVE THE SIBLINGS IN SHOCK

2415
01:28:19,127 --> 01:28:20,261
How loving can you be?

2416
01:28:20,328 --> 01:28:21,763
Sitting next to each other.

2417
01:28:21,829 --> 01:28:24,265
Or how you end up
rubbing on each other when you fight.

2418
01:28:24,332 --> 01:28:26,734
Right now, we're the most physical
we have ever been.

2419
01:28:27,969 --> 01:28:29,304
THE LOVING SISTERS' SPICY TWIST

2420
01:28:29,370 --> 01:28:30,605
You eat it all, pig!

2421
01:28:31,472 --> 01:28:32,607
THE SPICY SISTERS

2422
01:28:32,674 --> 01:28:34,242
PRESENT THEIR FRIDGE

2423
01:28:34,309 --> 01:28:35,643
We love spicy food so much.

2424
01:28:35,710 --> 01:28:37,111
Aren't these really spicy?

2425
01:28:37,178 --> 01:28:38,012
Do you not feel it?

2426
01:28:38,079 --> 01:28:39,147
Is there anything spicier?

2427
01:28:39,480 --> 01:28:41,916
FOR THE SISTERS WHO LOVE THE RED FLAVOR,

2428
01:28:41,983 --> 01:28:44,819
ALL KINDS OF RED DISHES ARE SERVED

2429
01:28:44,886 --> 01:28:46,387
The sexy grandpa.

2430
01:28:46,454 --> 01:28:47,655
Someone call 911.

2431
01:28:47,722 --> 01:28:48,990
That's insane.

2432
01:28:49,057 --> 01:28:50,491
That's going to kill you!

2433
01:28:50,558 --> 01:28:52,327
-I love it.
-It's too spicy.

2434
01:28:52,393 --> 01:28:53,828
THE SPICY SISTERS' EATING MODE

2435
01:28:53,895 --> 01:28:54,896
MMM

2436
01:28:54,962 --> 01:28:56,130
That's what I'm talking about.

2437
01:28:56,197 --> 01:28:57,098
It looks so good.

2438
01:28:57,265 --> 01:28:58,266
THE SISTERS' MUKBANG

2439
01:28:59,567 --> 01:29:00,902
WHICH CHEF CAPTURED THE APPETITE

2440
01:29:01,135 --> 01:29:02,437
OF THESE TWO SISTERS?

2441
01:29:05,973 --> 01:29:08,009
They seem quite unrivaled.

2442
01:29:08,576 --> 01:29:10,044
You have that distinct color.

2443
01:29:10,978 --> 01:29:13,848
-What do you mean by "distinct color"?
-We are colored, yes.

2444
01:29:13,915 --> 01:29:16,150
-I mean, we're all colored.
-You'll get canceled.

2445
01:29:16,217 --> 01:29:18,052
-It's not that.
-You'd better be careful.

2446
01:29:27,295 --> 01:29:32,300
Subtitle translation by: Eunsook Youn
